  /* ===== Help dialog (rewritten 2026-10-28): whole HTML lives here ===== */
  "help.title": "Save Sync · Help",
  "help.what": '<div class="hq"><h4>What this is</h4><p>An interactive map for <i>The Legend of Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom</i> — sky / surface / depths layers, collection tracking and live player navigation.</p></div>',
  "help.path": '<div class="hq"><h4>① Where the save file is</h4><p>The file is <code>progress.sav</code>; <code>slot_00</code> ~ <code>slot_05</code> are the six in-game save slots:</p><p>Ryujinx: <code>%APPDATA%\\Ryujinx\\bis\\user\\save\\…\\slot_00\\progress.sav</code></p><p>Eden: under the emulator folder, <code>user\\nand\\user\\save\\…\\slot_00\\progress.sav</code></p><p>If you run <b class="hl">TOTKNavi</b> you can open the save folder right from the app — no need to hunt for it.</p></div>',
  "help.load": '<div class="hq"><h4>② Two ways to load</h4><ul><li><b class="hl">Automatic (recommended)</b>: start TOTKNavi — once you save in-game, the map syncs by itself.</li><li><b class="hl">Manual</b>: click "Load Save Progress" and pick <code>progress.sav</code>.</li></ul></div>',
  "help.data": '<div class="hq"><h4>③ What gets read</h4><p>Real progress for <b class="hl">20+ categories</b>: shrines, lightroots, skyview towers, koroks, chests, compendium, boss kills and more.</p><p><b>Not</b> readable: inventory counts (weapons / bows / shields / armor) and quest rewards — the save file does not store them.</p></div>',
  "help.privacy": '<div class="hq"><h4>④ Privacy</h4><p>The file is parsed entirely in your browser memory. <b class="hl">Nothing is uploaded.</b></p></div>',
  "help.more": '<div class="hq"><h4>⑤ More</h4><ul><li>Full docs, desktop navigator, changelog: <a href="https://github.com/yalincc/totkmap" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/yalincc/totkmap</a></li><li>Online map: <a href="https://totk.yalin.site" target="_blank" rel="noopener">totk.yalin.site</a></li></ul></div>',
  "swHelp.title": "Depths Pristine Weapon (✨) Mechanics",
  "swHelp.content": '<div class="hq"><h4>① Breaking Requirement</h4><p>Pristine weapons only unlock after finding and <b>fully breaking</b> their decayed counterparts on the surface. Until broken, default low-tier weapons (Traveler/Soldier) spawn.</p></div><div class="hq"><h4>② Hierarchical Pool (Why multiple candidates?)</h4><p>Pristine pillars include lower tier candidates (e.g. Royal pillars pool Royal/Knight/Soldier/Traveler). Lower tiers may still roll, which is why save-scumming is useful.</p></div><div class="hq"><h4>③ Must Remove Weapon for Blood Moon</h4><p>If the current weapon is left on the soldier, Blood Moons will <b>NOT reset it</b>! You MUST remove it via Ultrahand or pick it up so the ghost fades away.</p></div><div class="hq"><h4>④ Dual Save-Scumming (SL) Tips</h4><p>• <b>Reroll Weapon Type</b>: Types lock at 80-100m render distance. Save beyond 100m before approaching.<br>• <b>Reroll Modifiers</b>: Modifiers roll upon picking up. Save right before grabbing to reroll yellow bonuses (+10 Attack Up).</p></div><div class="hq"><h4>⑤ Weapon Series Passive Traits</h4><ul><li><b class="hl">Royal Guard</b>: 2x Attack when badly damaged (Base dur 12, Lynel killer)</li><li><b class="hl">Royal</b>: 2x Rush attack after Flurry Rush</li><li><b class="hl">Zora</b>: 2x Attack when wet / hydrated</li><li><b class="hl">Gerudo</b>: 2x Fuse material attack power (Lower dur)</li><li><b class="hl">Knight</b>: 2x Attack at 1 heart or less</li><li><b class="hl">Cobble</b>: Specialized for breaking rocks & ore</li><li><b class="hl">Forest</b>: Repeated burst / spray with attached fruits</li><li><b class="hl">Eightfold</b>: 8x Sneakstrike attack / wind slashes</li><li><b class="hl">Feathered</b>: Quick swings / wind gusts</li></ul></div><div class="hq"><h4>⑥ Surface Decayed Weapons (Break Requirement · Click to Locate)</h4><p>Pick up and <b>completely break</b> the decayed counterpart on the surface to unlock pristine versions in the Depths (Blood Moon respawns, click to locate):</p><ul><li><b class="hl">Royal Guard\'s Claymore</b>: <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="sw-locate-link" data-id="4057">📍Zelda\'s Room Fireplace (Hyrule Castle)</a></li><li><b class="hl">Royal Guard\'s Sword</b>: <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="sw-locate-link" data-id="8701">📍Zelda\'s Desk (Hyrule Castle)</a></li><li><b class="hl">Royal Guard\'s Spear</b>: <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="sw-locate-link" data-id="8702">📍Zelda\'s Corridor (Hyrule Castle)</a></li><li><b class="hl">Royal Claymore</b>: <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="sw-locate-link" data-id="8703">📍Observation Room (Hyrule Castle)</a></li><li><b class="hl">Royal Broadsword</b>: <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="sw-locate-link" data-id="8704">📍Gatehouse Outside Main Gate</a></li><li><b class="hl">Zora Spear</b>: <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="sw-locate-link" data-id="8705">📍Zora\'s Domain Pool Bottom</a></li><li><b class="hl">Zora Sword</b>: <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="sw-locate-link" data-id="8706">📍Ploymus Mountain / Toto Lake</a></li><li><b class="hl">Gerudo Claymore</b>: <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="sw-locate-link" data-id="8707">📍Kara Kara Bazaar Watchtower</a></li><li><b class="hl">Gerudo Scimitar</b>: <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="sw-locate-link" data-id="8708">📍Gerudo Town Outskirts</a></li><li><b class="hl">Cobble Crusher</b>: <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="sw-locate-link" data-id="8709">📍Southern Mine Track Box</a></li><li><b class="hl">Forest Dweller\'s Sword</b>: <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="sw-locate-link" data-id="8710">📍Minshi Woods Campfire</a></li><li><b class="hl">Feathered Edge</b>: <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="sw-locate-link" data-id="8711">📍Rito Flight Range Table</a></li></ul></div>',
